@startuml stack
' Mail stack — Thunderbird as the credential-holding proxy (2026-08-14).
' The decision drawn as a picture: ONE program owns credentials, network
' and every write; the CLI reads through file seams only. Pink is the
' entire bespoke surface (one query catalog); everything else is
' off-the-shelf. The Gloda cylinder is private Thunderbird internals
' with an announced successor (Panorama) — the read path is built to be
' deleted, which is why it is one pink box and not an architecture.
title Mail stack — Thunderbird proxy: one writer, file seams for reading
caption cylinder = working data, rebuilt on demand (gold = Thunderbird-owned, never written by us) · file = authored/irreplaceable truth · pink = our own code (the entire bespoke surface) · solid = runs today · dashed = next in the catalog, slots into the same interfaces

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam linetype ortho

actor "user" as user
cloud "Gmail\n(IMAP/SMTP + OAuth2)" as gmail

file "git identity\nuser.name / user.email —\nONE identity source,\nread by provisioning and\nreply-audit alike" as gitid #Honeydew

note as oauthnote
  the ONLY manual step in the whole
  stack: one OAuth consent click at
  first connect. The account itself
  is seeded from the git identity —
  the setup wizard never runs.
end note

[Thunderbird\nofficial tarball — holds credentials,\nsyncs, sends, renders; the ONE writer] as tb
oauthnote .. tb

[BuxarTranslate\nGoogle Translate add-on] as buxar
[Thunderbird Translate\nGemini add-on] as ttrans
note as transnote
  two DISSIMILAR cloud translators —
  one service degrading doesn't take
  both. Stated trade-off: selected
  text reaches Google. Both retire
  the day Thunderbird ships its
  on-device engine (Bergamot, on
  the official roadmap).
end note
transnote .. buxar

database "profile user.js\nseeded prefs: account graph,\nindexer pin — read at startup,\nnever fought over with a\nlive Thunderbird" as userjs #Gold
database "global-messages-db.sqlite\nGloda full-text index —\nprivate schema, dies with\nPanorama, priced in" as gloda #Gold

[mail query catalog\nsearch / unanswered / ad-hoc SQL —\none pattern rule, questions as data] as catalog #Pink
note as catnote
  read-only at the CONNECTION level
  (sqlite mode=ro) — "nothing but
  Thunderbird writes" is a mechanism,
  not a promise. The reply audit
  answers "which lawyer threads
  await my reply?" from the same
  seam. The whole Gloda vocabulary
  lives in this one deletable file.
end note
catnote .. catalog

[terminal / agent\nanswers on stdout] as term

' dormant tier: adopted the day a live verb is needed (YAGNI)
[thunderbird-cli\nsigned extension bridge —\nsupported API, live freshness,\ndraft-gated sending] as bridge
note as bridgenote
  next in the catalog: the SUPPORTED
  scripting surface. Slots in when a
  question needs what files cannot
  give — live state, full message
  bodies, replying. The catalog
  interface survives; only the
  queries retarget.
end note
bridgenote .. bridge

gitid --> tb : provisioning seeds the\naccount pref graph
gmail <--> tb : OAuth once, then\nsync + send
userjs --> tb : read at startup
tb --> gloda : background indexer\n(only while running —\nautostart keeps it fresh)
buxar --> tb : translate selection
ttrans --> tb : translate message

gloda --> catalog : read-only
catalog --> term

tb ..> bridge : pending consumer
bridge ..> term : live verbs, when needed

user --> tb : reads + writes mail —\nthe ONLY write surface
term --> user : sees: search hits,\nopen-thread audit
tb --> user : one OAuth click,\nonce

' layout: cloud north, user east of the seams
gmail -[hidden]down-> tb
tb -[hidden]right-> user
gloda -[hidden]right-> catalog
@enduml
